          "create_time": 1792864204.193,
          "update_time": 1792864205.575,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The complex form also shortens the current and continuity law. I’ve checked that it preserves the signs and constants in \\(\\eqref{eq:SP}\\), and that a \\(45^\\circ\\) rotation gives the complex-potential DS-II form in the manuscript’s cited source. Real coordinates remain useful for seeing the kinetic operator’s indefinite sign.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
